{
  "core": "Creation moves what has ripened into form across the threshold and releases it outward. In Wisdom, it works on the held knowing itself — the sealed store of what deep thought has gathered. Overdone, the releasing floods the holding: everything gets pushed across before it has finished gathering, and the threshold becomes a trap door. Nothing stays long enough to become whole.",
  "sheetLine": "The door opens before the fruit is ripe; nothing stays whole enough to leave."
